  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe makes 4"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "okonomiyaki"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "pancakes and takes around 35 minutes. Each pancake is thick, layered with shredded cabbage, pork belly, and spring onions, and cooked until the outside is golden and the inside just set. They are topped with okonomiyaki sauce,"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Japanese mayonnaise"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ","
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "bonito flakes"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", and"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "aonori"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The batter should be thick and only just bound together. The cabbage and other fillings make up most of the volume. Do not overmix once the wet and dry ingredients are combined. The turning step is the trickiest part. Use a wide spatula and move with confidence. A hesitant flip often breaks the pancake in two."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
